  "text": "DERPEX production-readiness run (2026-08-29). Branch production-readiness, plan at docs/plans/2026-08-29-production-readiness.md.\n\nPatterns that worked:\n- Parallel opus implementers in worktrees with strict file-ownership lists, then one opus/sonnet reviewer per branch, then SendMessage follow-ups to the SAME agent (context intact). Reviewers found real bugs every single time (mesh key raw in supervisor init args; chmod 0700 of operator dirs; Ring.delete without closed flag; count-cap≠wire-cap silent billing loss; yield tier unbounded under load). Never merge without the review.\n- Merge gotcha: `git checkout --theirs` on a conflicted test file silently drops the other branch's edits to that file (lost A1's Secret.wrap + server_public_key in go_client_test). Rebuild from the richer side + port the smaller change instead.\n- Supervisors retain init args → wrapping a secret at the child-spec boundary is too late; wrap before the spec exists (Application).\n- BEAM: :ssl.close is a gen_statem call into a connection whose tls_sender is blocked → can't be used as a write-timeout watchdog; inet send_timeout on the underlying gen_tcp DOES surface as {:error,:timeout} from :ssl.send (tls_sender.erl ~592). Verified by two independent agents.\n- BEAM: :ssl.handshake/3 with options doesn't wrap the paused {ok,Ext} reply in OTP 29 — use handshake: :hello in LISTEN options + :ssl.handshake/1 + handshake_continue.\n- BEAM: :file.open on a directory is :eisdir → no directory fsync from Elixir.\n- :erlang.yield is unbounded in load (4µs idle → 39ms at 400 runnable); never use yield loops as a \"cheap\" tier; bound by wall clock.\n- ETS ordered_set with partially bound tuple key select IS a range scan under write_concurrency CA tree (12µs vs 22ms for set at 200k rows).\n- StreamData binary(max_length:) is capped by generation size (~runs); use integer(range) + binary(length:) to reach caps.\n- Machine load hit 150 with 7 concurrent agent test suites → wall-clock tests flake; always rerun failures in isolation before believing them.\n- test.all/release.check aliases were decorative and release.yml had no test dependency — check gates actually run the suite.",
  "sections": [
    "Project Notes"
  ],
